\b Google Ads API - Design Documentation (Keyword Ideas Tool)\b0\par
\par
\b Document owner:\b0 ALT-F-AWESOME / Geldgeregeld.nl\par
\b Date:\b0 2026-02-16\par
\b Version:\b0 1.0\par
\par
\b 1. Purpose and scope\b0\par
This document describes the design of an internal tool that uses the Google Ads API KeywordPlanIdeaService to generate keyword ideas (including long-tail keyword candidates) and associated historical metrics. The output is used to support SEO content planning and paid search campaign planning.\par
\par
\b In scope:\b0\par
- Generate keyword ideas from seed keywords and/or a seed URL\par
- Apply simple filters (e.g., max average monthly searches) to focus on long-tail candidates\par
- Export results to CSV for internal review\par
\par
\b Out of scope:\b0\par
- Automatic campaign creation or bid changes\par
- Storing or processing personally identifiable information (PII)\par
- User-facing public API\par
\par
\b 2. High-level architecture\b0\par
The tool is implemented as a Node.js script executed by internal operators on a developer machine or CI runner. It calls the Google Ads API over HTTPS and writes results to a local CSV file.\par
\par
\b Components:\b0\par
- Operator: runs the script with seeds and optional filters\par
- Node.js script: constructs request and calls Google Ads API\par
- Google Ads API: KeywordPlanIdeaService (GenerateKeywordIdeas)\par
\par
\b 3. Intended users\b0\par
Internal marketing/SEO operators and engineering staff. There is no public end-user access.\par
\par
\b 4. Key use cases\b0\par
\b 4.1 Generate long-tail keyword candidates\b0\par
Input: a list of seed keywords (e.g., "lijfrente zzp") and/or a relevant landing page URL.\par
Output: keyword ideas with historical metrics. The operator filters by average monthly searches (e.g., <= 200) to surface long-tail queries.\par
\par
\b 4.2 Account sanity check\b0\par
The tool can list accessible customers (customers:listAccessibleCustomers) to verify account access before generating keyword ideas.\par
\par
\b 5. Data flow\b0\par
\b Inputs:\b0\par
- Seed keywords and/or seed URL (operator-supplied)\par
- Targeting: language constant and geo target constants\par
- Google Ads customer id and optional login customer id (manager account)\par
\par
\b Processing:\b0\par
1) Authenticate to Google Ads API (see Section 6)\par
2) Call customers:listAccessibleCustomers (optional)\par
3) Call GenerateKeywordIdeas with selected seeds and targeting\par
4) Extract keyword idea text and metrics from response\par
5) Apply optional numeric filters on avgMonthlySearches to emphasize long-tail candidates\par
6) Write results to a CSV file for internal analysis\par
\par
\b Outputs:\b0\par
- CSV with keyword ideas and metrics (avgMonthlySearches, competition, bid estimates)\par
- Console logs for operational visibility (counts, errors)\par
\par
\b 6. Authentication and authorization\b0\par
The tool uses a service account with Domain-Wide Delegation (DWD) and impersonates a Google Workspace user who has access to the relevant Google Ads accounts.\par
\par
\b Auth method:\b0\par
- OAuth2 service account JWT flow with subject impersonation (DWD)\par
- Scope: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/adwords\par
\par
\b Authorization model:\b0\par
- The impersonated Workspace user must have access to the Google Ads customer account(s)\par
- For access to client accounts under a manager account, the tool can set the login-customer-id header\par
\par
\b Secrets:\b0\par
- Google Ads API developer token is provided via environment variables (not hardcoded)\par
- Service account JSON key is stored as a secret on the operator machine or in a secret manager (not committed to source control)\par
\par
\b 7. Security and compliance\b0\par
\b 7.1 Sensitive data handling\b0\par
- No PII is collected, transmitted, or stored.\par
- The tool requests only keyword planning data and metrics.\par
\par
\b 7.2 Credential storage\b0\par
- Credentials are provided at runtime via environment variables or secret storage.\par
- Secrets are excluded from version control.\par
\par
\b 7.3 Access control\b0\par
- Tool execution is restricted to internal operators.\par
- Least privilege: only adwords scope required to call the keyword planning endpoints.\par
\par
\b 8. Error handling and monitoring\b0\par
- HTTP errors are surfaced to the operator with relevant response snippets.\par
- The tool is designed to fail fast on missing configuration.\par
\par
\b 9. Rate limits and usage controls\b0\par
- The tool requests a bounded page size and supports limiting output.\par
- Operators run the tool on demand; it is not a high-frequency background job.\par
\par
\b 10. Testing\b0\par
- Manual smoke testing by listing accessible customers and running a small keyword idea request.\par
- Validation that generated CSV output is parseable and contains expected fields.\par
\par
\b 11. Deployment and operations\b0\par
- Run locally using Node.js (>=18).\par
- Configuration is provided via .env.local on the operator machine.\par
\par
\b 12. Change management\b0\par
- Changes to request parameters (language/geo/network) are reviewed by engineering.\par
- Credential rotation is handled separately from code changes.\par
\par
\b Appendix A: Configuration fields (examples)\b0\par
(Do not include real secrets in submissions.)\par
- GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN="..." \par
- GOOGLE_ADS_CUSTOMER_ID="..." \par
- GOOGLE_ADS_LOGIN_CUSTOMER_ID="..." (optional) \par
- GOOGLE_ADS_IMPERSONATED_EMAIL="daniel@altfawesome.com" \par
\par
